<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Nekor</h1><p class="st-meta">710 CE – 1019 CE (approx.) · capital Nekor</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Islamic principality in Morocco, ruled by an Arab dynasty on the Rif coast for three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 710 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> granted the coastal region of the Rif to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salih-ibn-mansur">Salih ibn Mansur</a>, an Arab of Himyarite descent who preached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> to the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribes. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/salihids">Salihids</a>, ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, and his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ibn-idris">Said ibn Idris</a> built the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekor">Nekor</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hoceima">Al Hoceima</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekor">Nekor</a> was a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki school</a>, based on farming in the Nekor valley and trade across the sea with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. It suffered a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raid around 859 and the Fatimid sack of the city in 917, after which the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/salihids">Salihids</a> returned with Andalusian help. They recognised the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Umayyad Caliphate of Córdoba</a> as overlord in the 10th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the early 11th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> had lost its independence amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zenata Berber</a> wars, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekor">Nekor</a> in 1080. Its role as the Rif's main port passed to other towns.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-nekor.jpg" alt="Emirate of Nekor" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: Omar-Toons; derivative work by Stegop · CC BY 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_pol%C3%ADtico_de_Marrocos_(s%C3%A9c._VIII-XI).gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>710 CE – 1019 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nekor</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Salih ibn Mansur, Said ibn Idris</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Nekor, Salihids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=864&amp;focus=emirate-of-nekor" aria-label="Emirate of Nekor on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4584 909 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Nekor lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4904 1165L6134 1224M4904 1165L4881 1071M4904 1165L4799 1289"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0M4881 1071h0M4799 1289h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4904 1165h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4904 1165h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nekor. <a href="/atlas?year=864&amp;focus=emirate-of-nekor">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

